# The log is the machine's state, not code.
last-run.log
last-run.log.old

# A copy of damaged settings: the diagnostics of one incident.
settings.json.bad

# The cache of compiled types. Built from the source in DisplayCore.ps1.
native-*.dll

# Images for the eye: the icon preview from Make-Icon.ps1 and the window images from
# render-preview.ps1. Both scripts are development tools, and their output is not code.
preview.png
preview-*.png

# Window-position snapshots: HWNDs live only within one logon.
window-state.json

# The last chosen mode: the machine's state, changing on every switch.
last-mode.json

# The monitors' verified modes: the resolution and refresh rate this machine really showed.
# Needed to set a sleeping monitor's mode in one transition.
display-modes.json

# Personal settings: the set of monitors, the shortcut bindings and the order on the desk are
# everybody's own. Only settings.example.json lives in the repository, and this file is created
# by itself on the first run.
settings.json

# The diary: how much time in which application, on which monitor and in which mode. Data about a
# person rather than about the program — it must not go into the repository. The file is only
# created when the diary is turned on in the settings, and it can be deleted.
activity.json

# The diary's report. Overwritten on every opening of "Statistics…".
stats.html

# The built release and its hash — tools\pack.ps1 makes them out of what is already in the
# repository. Committing the archive would mean storing the contents twice, the second time in a
# form that cannot be edited.
ScreenDeck-*.zip*

# The release notes: the extract from CHANGELOG.md that pack.ps1 prepares for the release page.
# The original is CHANGELOG.md itself.
release-notes.md
